    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d771">

                <pb facs="0836" n="716" sameAs="frus:frus1931v02/pg716"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">411.12 Gomez and Rubio/49</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Mexican Chargé</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Herrera
                            de Huerta</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-06-24">June 24, 1931</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: The receipt is acknowledged of your note of
                    June 16, 1931,<anchor n="16" xml:id="d771-f1"/> with further reference to the
                    unfortunate shooting at Ardmore, Oklahoma, of the young Mexican students, Emilio
                    Cortés Rubio and Manuel García Gómez. You inform the Department that the
                    Ministry of Foreign Relations of Mexico considers it desirable that the
                    necessary investigations be continued by the Governor of the State of
                    Oklahoma.</p>
                <pb facs="0837" n="717" xml:id="pg717"/>
                <p>According to the Department’s information, the authorities of the State of
                    Oklahoma are pursuing the investigation of this case with all due despatch
                    required by law.</p>
                <p>Accept [etc.]</p>
                <closer>For the Secretary of State:<lb/><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">James
                            Grafton Rogers</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
